{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1540310-w20-rite-of-the-questing-stone-questions","id":1540310,"title":"W20 Rite of the Questing Stone questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-08-13T16:37:17-07:00","id":1540310,"title":"W20 Rite of the Questing Stone questions","content":"Greeetings,<br /> <br /> Some questions related to the Rite of the Questing Stone on W20:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>What happens if you have a fake name or an alias for the target? Is it an autofail without any feedback? Does it tell you that the target name is invalid?</li> <li>What happens if the target is in another plane?</li> <li>If the target is dead does it work finding the body (assuming one exists) or the ghost? Does it autofail?</li> <li>How specific do you have to be to find someone? If you know the name but never met the person?</li> </ol>Bonus question. Descent Into the Underworld rite. How do you return from the Underworld? The rite sends you there, but there is no return option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-13T20:43:17-07:00","id":1540327,"title":"","content":"This is how I would handle it in chronicles that I ST.<br /> <br /> 1) If the person was known by others by that fake name or alias (you ask for &quot;Sting&quot; instead of &quot;Gordon Sumner&quot;), then the rite works as normal. If it was a one time alias other people don't recognize, then it wouldn't. If it is something that sometimes gets used or is known by a limited range of people, I'd just roll with a slightly higher difficulty. Whatever the ST is comfortable with and can justify to her players.<br /> <br /> 2) I would not have it work, but probably do something like having the stone (or compass, or whatever is used in the rite) keep spinning so that the characters recognize it is an odd response that is not normal. Most Garou would probably recognize what that response signifies.<br /> <br /> 3) I would have it find the dead body or grave. I would not have the rite find ghosts or spirits, but need to be something from this physical world. If the person has been dead so long that the body is no longer recognizable as the person it once, I would not have the rite work. The stone or compass would just be still.<br /> <br /> 4) The rite just says the name, so even if that is all you have, I would still have the rite work. However, you only get the general location (eventually, it may take some time for the rite to lead you to the correct location), not its exact position. So if the rite leads the ritemaster to a crowded square, the ritemaster still has to distinguish the correct individual from the mass of people there. So if you just have the name, you may be out of luck. Also, if there are multiple people known by that name, and all you have is the name, the ritemaster may get the wrong person.<br /> <br /> I figure whatever powers the rite is knowledgeable, but not omniscient. It's the equivalent of a search engine, so the less the ritemaster knows about the intended target, the more likely it is to produce a wrong result or fail. It is a powerful rite for what it is, but it is still only a level one rite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":".  typo 09-16-2024, 03:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T06:59:17-07:00","id":1540350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1540310-w20-rite-of-the-questing-stone-questions?p=1540327#post1540327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is how I would handle it in chronicles that I ST.<br /> <br /> 1) If the person was known by others by that fake name or alias (you ask for &quot;Sting&quot; instead of &quot;Gordon Sumner&quot;), then the rite works as normal. If it was a one time alias other people don't recognize, then it wouldn't. If it is something that sometimes gets used or is known by a limited range of people, I'd just roll with a slightly higher difficulty. Whatever the ST is comfortable with and can justify to her players.<br /> <br /> 2) I would not have it work, but probably do something like having the stone (or compass, or whatever is used in the rite) keep spinning so that the characters recognize it is an odd response that is not normal. Most Garou would probably recognize what that response signifies.<br /> <br /> 3) I would have it find the dead body or grave. I would not have the rite find ghosts or spirits, but need to be something from this physical world. If the person has been dead so long that the body is no longer recognizable as the person it once, I would not have the rite work. The stone or compass would just be still.<br /> <br /> 4) The rite just says the name, so even if that is all you have, I would still have the rite work. However, you only get the general location (eventually, it may take some time for the rite to lead you to the correct location), not its exact position. So if the rite leads the ritemaster to a crowded square, the ritemaster still has to distinguish the correct individual from the mass of people there. So if you just have the name, you may be out of luck. Also, if there are multiple people known by that name, and all you have is the name, the ritemaster may get the wrong person.<br /> <br /> I figure whatever powers the right is knowledgeable, but not omniscient. It's the equivalent of a search engine, so the less the ritemaster knows about the intended target, the more likely it is to produce a wrong result or fail. It is a powerful rite for what it is, but it is still only a level one rite.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the answers, do you have any opinions on the Descent Into Underworld rite? My final question? Thanks again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T09:32:17-07:00","id":1540364,"title":"","content":"That's a good question. Something basic like that not being included in the rite is a good test to see if the writers ever play tested these things rather than just had a neat idea.<br /> <br /> Obviously the Garou must be capable of returning to the living world as a result of that rite, otherwise the rite would be useless. The question is when and where it happens.<br /> <br /> The original rite of Descent into the Dark Umbra was introduced in the first Silent Strider tribebook I believe. The general description is about the same, but not identical. The second tribebook version is obviously the basis for the W20 corebook version, but slightly edited. Neither tells us anything about returning.<br /> <br /> However, the Silver Fangs tribebooks also have a similar rite used by the Ivory Priesthood. The result is the same (Garou enters the underworld), but the flavor text and mechanics are very different. But that rite (also level 3) includes a time limit - the Garou may remain in the underworld until the next morning/dawn. The second tribebook adds a twist: &quot;If she fails to return to the material world by dawn the next morning, she is trapped in the Dark Umbra unless another Ivory Priest or a kindly Silent Strider helps her back across into the material world.&quot;<br /> <br /> So personally I would use this other Silver Fang rite (alternatively called Enter Dark Umbra or Walking with the Dead) as the basis for Descent of the Underworld. These would be the points I would tell the players.<br /> <br /> 1) Garou who enter the Underworld can stay only until dawn of the next morning. That is the time limit on how long they can stay.<br /> <br /> 2) Garou wishing to return to the land of the living only need to return to the spot they entered in the Underworld (the Shadowlands spot they originally entered) that correspond to where the sigils in the ground were drawn. Simply by willing it, the Garou returns to the living world but then cannot enter the underworld again unless the Rite is performed again. They cannot will themselves back unless they are at the spot where the gate was originally opened.<br /> <br /> 3) Garou MUST return to the spot in the Shadowlands and will themselves back to the land of the living before dawn the next morning or they will be trapped there unless rescued by more Garou sent by the rite to recover them.<br /> <br /> I like that last bit simply because escaping the land of the dead is generally perilous so having a penalty for not obeying the laws is good for me. Some STs won't want to bother with that for whatever reasons of convenience or taste, and if so I would then just have the Garou expelled forcefully the moment dawn hits. Perhaps taking some damage as a consequence.<br /> <br /> I think these rules provide a clear answer for players and have great flavor text that players would accept. Other STs might have other ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":".  typo 09-16-2024, 03:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}